{
 "_comment": [
  "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code to English name, for every country that gets boards.",
  "",
  "Only the code and the name are here. The Wikidata QID for each is resolved at",
  "build time and cached — 190-odd QIDs written from memory would be wrong",
  "somewhere, and a wrong country QID produces a full board of the wrong",
  "nationality with nothing to show it went wrong.",
  "",
  "'tier' decides the size: 2 gets the extended taxonomy (150 boards, 50",
  "contenders each), 1 gets core plus its regional blocks (about 50 boards, 10",
  "contenders each).",
  "'demonyms' is what a board is actually titled: 'Greatest British Cricketer', not 'Greatest United Kingdom Cricketer'."
 ],
 "tiers": {
  "US": 2,
  "IN": 2
